ction is configured by driver. But we can indicate flags.\n\nThus overlay:\n\n/ {\n    i2c0: i2c@... ??? Actually on native_sim, i2c0 node is something like i2c0: i2c@0 { ... };\n\nBut we can just overlay using &i2c0 { status = \"okay\"; bme680: bme680@77 { compatible = \"bosch,bme680\"; reg = <0x77>; status = \"okay\"; }; };\n\nSimilarly for &spi0 { status = \"okay\"; spi_nor_flash: flash@0 { compatible = \"jedec,spi-nor\"; reg = <0>; spi-max-frequency = <8000000>; size = <0x200000>; status = \"okay\"; }; };\n\nFor gpio0: &gpio0 { status = \"okay\"; named-gpios = <&gpio0 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>, <&gpio0 5 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; };\n\nMake sure include angle brackets, and maybe specify \"GPIO_OUTPUT\" flags? Actually for output we could add GPIO_OUTPUT in flags, but typical use: <&gpio0 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>. Output/input not part.\n\nThus final output. Provide only the file content."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"queue_time": 0.01744827, "prompt_tokens": 255, "prompt_time": 0.010376616, "completion_tokens": 722, "completion_time": 1.520670628, "total_tokens": 977, "total_time": 1.531047244, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 517}}, "usage_breakdown": null, "system_fingerprint": "fp_49bfac06f1", "x_groq": {"id": "req_01ktj153wbews906vyjzznp7fm", "seed": 2115540632}, "service_tier": "on_demand"}


